      en: "The Rauma River flows 68 kilometers through the Romsdal region, draining Lake Lesjaskogsvatnet into the Romsdalsfjord. Its catchment area spans 1,210 km². Known for its emerald waters, the river passes through the dramatic Slettafossen gorge. The river supports a renowned salmon fishery, with annual catches exceeding 1,500 kg. The Raumabanen railway, opened in 1924, follows the river valley. Average discharge is 40 m³/s, with spring floods peaking at 300 m³/s. The river is also a key site for white-water kayaking.",
